tel 1.0

# The terms fuel's own documents name in brackets: each with a definition shown when the term
# is pointed at, and a link to the page which explains it in full.

define fence
  link  /doc/doc/markdown.md#fenced-code
  definition
      A block of code in a Markdown document, between lines of three backticks, whose first
      line names its language; Fuel highlights it, and compiles it when it is Scala.

define preamble
  link  /doc/doc/markdown.md#a-preamble
  definition
      The TEL at the start of a ` ```scala fuel ` fence, ended by a line holding `##`, which
      says how the fence is compiled, marked and animated.

define glossary
  definition
      The terms a documentation site explains in a sentence or two, defined in a TEL file and
      shown when a bracketed term in prose is pointed at.
